**Transactions:**

```java
// Transaction management
@Service
public class UserService {
    
    @Autowired
    private UserRepository userRepository;
    
    // Transaction required (default) - starts new or joins existing
    @Transactional
    public void transferMoney(Long fromUserId, Long toUserId, BigDecimal amount) {
        User fromUser = userRepository.findById(fromUserId).orElseThrow();
        User toUser = userRepository.findById(toUserId).orElseThrow();
        
        fromUser.setBalance(fromUser.getBalance().subtract(amount));
        toUser.setBalance(toUser.getBalance().add(amount));
        
        userRepository.save(fromUser);
        userRepository.save(toUser);
        // Automatic commit if no exception
        // Automatic rollback if exception thrown
    }
    
    // Read-only transaction (optimization - no dirty checking)
    @Transactional(readOnly = true)
    public UserDTO getUserDetails(Long id) {
        return userRepository.findById(id)
            .map(this::convertToDTO)
            .orElseThrow(() -> new ResourceNotFoundException("User not found"));
    }
    
    // Custom propagation
    @Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRES_NEW)
    public void logAction(String action) {
        // Always creates new transaction
        // Outer transaction suspended, continues after this
    }
    
    // Isolation level
    @Transactional(isolation = Isolation.READ_COMMITTED)
    public void criticalOperation() {
        // Higher isolation level prevents dirty reads
    }
}

/*
Propagation levels:
- REQUIRED: Start transaction or join existing (DEFAULT)
- REQUIRES_NEW: Always create new transaction
- SUPPORTS: Use existing transaction if available
- NOT_SUPPORTED: Don't use transaction
- NEVER: Throw exception if transaction exists
- MANDATORY: Transaction must exist

Isolation levels:
- READ_UNCOMMITTED: Can read uncommitted changes (dirty reads)
- READ_COMMITTED: Cannot read uncommitted changes (default)
- REPEATABLE_READ: Repeated reads get same result
- SERIALIZABLE: Complete isolation, slowest
*/
```

**Key Benefits:**
- Automatic SQL generation from method names
- Type-safe database queries
- Transaction management and consistency
- Pagination and sorting out-of-box
- Lazy and eager loading strategies
- Clear separation of concerns

