## Security

**Theory:**
Security in Spring Boot is handled by Spring Security framework, which provides authentication (verifying who you are) and authorization (verifying what you can do). It offers multiple authentication strategies including form-based, JWT tokens, OAuth2, and more. Security is crucial for protecting sensitive data and preventing unauthorized access.

**Fundamental Security Concepts:**

**Authentication (Who are you?):**
- Verifying user identity
- Username/password validation
- Multi-factor authentication
- OAuth2/SAML integration
- Biometric authentication
- Techniques: Sessions, Tokens (JWT), API keys

**Authorization (What can you do?):**
- Verifying user permissions
- Role-based access control (RBAC)
- Attribute-based access control (ABAC)
- Permission-based control
- Techniques: Role checking, ACLs, policy files

**Key Concepts:**
- **Authentication**: Verifying user identity (login)
- **Authorization**: Determining access permissions (what user can do)
- **Roles**: Groups of permissions assigned to users (ADMIN, USER, GUEST)
- **Authorities**: Individual permissions that can be granted
- **JWT Tokens**: Stateless authentication for APIs (JSON Web Token)
- **Session Management**: Tracking authenticated users
- **CSRF Protection**: Prevent cross-site request forgery
- **Password Hashing**: Never store plain text passwords
- **Filter Chain**: Security filters execute in specific order
- **Stateless vs Stateful**: Sessions vs tokens

**Security Architecture:**
- Authenticate user (login)
- Create security context
- Store principal in ThreadLocal
- Check authorization on each request
- Execute business logic
- Generate response
- Clear context

**Key Points:**
- Multiple authentication mechanisms supported
- Authorization can be declarative or programmatic
- Default provides basic security (HTTPS enforcement, CSRF, etc.)
- Customizable for complex requirements
- Integration with databases for user/role storage
- Event-driven security (login, logout events)
- Spring Security filters integrate with servlet filters

**Spring Security Filter Chain:**

```
HTTP Request
    ↓
SecurityFilterChain (Multiple filters in order)
    ├── SecurityContextPersistenceFilter (Load from session)
    ├── LogoutFilter (Handle logout)
    ├── AuthenticationFilter (Handle login)
    ├── ExceptionTranslationFilter (Handle exceptions)
    └── FilterSecurityInterceptor (Check authorization)
    ↓
HTTP Response
```

**Basic Spring Security Configuration:**

```java
@Configuration
@EnableWebSecurity
public class SecurityConfig extends WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter {
    
    @Bean
    public PasswordEncoder passwordEncoder() {
        // Use BCrypt for password hashing
        // Never store plain text passwords
        return new BCryptPasswordEncoder();
    }
    
    @Override
    protected void configure(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
        http
            // Enable CSRF protection for form submissions
            .csrf()
            .and()
            
            // Authorization configuration
            .authorizeRequests()
                .antMatchers("/", "/signup", "/css/**").permitAll()  // Public endpoints
                .antMatchers("/admin/**").hasRole("ADMIN")           // Admin only
                .antMatchers("/user/**").hasAnyRole("USER", "ADMIN")// USER or ADMIN
                .anyRequest().authenticated()                        // All others require auth
            .and()
            
            // Form login configuration
            .formLogin()
                .loginPage("/login")                          // Custom login page
                .defaultSuccessUrl("/dashboard")              // Redirect after login
                .permitAll()
            .and()
            
            // Logout configuration
            .logout()
                .logoutUrl("/logout")
                .logoutSuccessUrl("/")
                .permitAll()
            .and()
            
            // Remember me functionality
            .rememberMe()
                .rememberMeParameter("remember-me")
                .tokenValiditySeconds(86400); // 24 hours
    }
}
```

**JWT Token-Based Authentication:**

```java
// JWT Token Provider - Generates and validates tokens
@Component
@Slf4j
public class JwtTokenProvider {
    
    @Value("${app.jwt-secret:secretKeyForJWT}")
    private String jwtSecret;
    
    @Value("${app.jwt-expiration:86400000}")  // 24 hours in milliseconds
    private long jwtExpirationMs;
    
    // Generate JWT token for authenticated user
    public String generateToken(UserDetails userDetails) {
        Map<String, Object> claims = new HashMap<>();
        claims.put("authorities", getAuthorities(userDetails));
        return createToken(claims, userDetails.getUsername());
    }
    
    // Create token with claims
    private String createToken(Map<String, Object> claims, String subject) {
        Date now = new Date();
        Date expiryDate = new Date(now.getTime() + jwtExpirationMs);
        
        return Jwts.builder()
                .setClaims(claims)
                .setSubject(subject)
                .setIssuedAt(now)
                .setExpiration(expiryDate)
                .signWith(SignatureAlgorithm.HS512, jwtSecret)  // Sign with secret
                .compact();
    }
    
    // Extract username from token
    public String getUsernameFromToken(String token) {
        return Jwts.parser()
                .setSigningKey(jwtSecret)
                .parseClaimsJws(token)
                .getBody()
                .getSubject();
    }
    
    // Validate token expiration and signature
    public boolean validateToken(String token) {
        try {
            Jwts.parser().setSigningKey(jwtSecret).parseClaimsJws(token);
            return true;
        } catch (JwtException ex) {
            log.error("Invalid JWT token: {}", ex.getMessage());
            return false;
        } catch (IllegalArgumentException ex) {
            log.error("JWT claims string is empty: {}", ex.getMessage());
            return false;
        }
    }
    
    private List<String> getAuthorities(UserDetails userDetails) {
        return userDetails.getAuthorities().stream()
                .map(GrantedAuthority::getAuthority)
                .collect(Collectors.toList());
    }
}

// JWT Authentication Filter - Intercepts requests with JWT
@Component
@Slf4j
public class JwtAuthenticationFilter extends OncePerRequestFilter {
    
    @Autowired
    private JwtTokenProvider tokenProvider;
    
    @Autowired
    private UserDetailsService userDetailsService;
    
    @Override
    protected void doFilterInternal(HttpServletRequest request,
            HttpServletResponse response,
            FilterChain filterChain) throws ServletException, IOException {
        try {
            // Extract JWT from request header
            String jwt = extractTokenFromRequest(request);
            
            // Validate and process token
            if (jwt != null && tokenProvider.validateToken(jwt)) {
                String username = tokenProvider.getUsernameFromToken(jwt);
                UserDetails userDetails = userDetailsService.loadUserByUsername(username);
                
                // Create authentication object
                UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken authentication =
                        new UsernamePasswordAuthenticationToken(
                                userDetails, 
                                null, 
                                userDetails.getAuthorities());
                
                // Set authentication in context
                SecurityContextHolder.getContext().setAuthentication(authentication);
            }
        } catch (Exception ex) {
            log.error("Could not set user authentication: {}", ex.getMessage());
        }
        
        // Continue filter chain
        filterChain.doFilter(request, response);
    }
    
    // Extract JWT from Authorization header
    private String extractTokenFromRequest(HttpServletRequest request) {
        String bearerToken = request.getHeader("Authorization");
        if (bearerToken != null && bearerToken.startsWith("Bearer ")) {
            return bearerToken.substring(7);  // Remove "Bearer " prefix
        }
        return null;
    }
}

