## Testing

**Theory:**
Testing is crucial for ensuring code quality, preventing regressions, and maintaining confidence in refactoring. Spring Boot provides excellent testing support with annotations like @SpringBootTest, @WebMvcTest, and @DataJpaTest. Tests should be fast, isolated, and focused on one behavior.

**Why Testing Matters:**
- Catches bugs early (cheaper to fix)
- Documents expected behavior
- Enables safe refactoring
- Builds confidence in code
- Catches edge cases
- Prevents regressions
- Improves code design (testable code is better designed)

**Testing Principles (FIRST):**
- **Fast**: Tests should run quickly
- **Independent**: Tests shouldn't depend on each other
- **Repeatable**: Same results every run
- **Self-checking**: Pass or fail automatically
- **Timely**: Written close to production code

**Test Scope Levels:**
1. **Unit Tests**: Single class/method in isolation (fastest)
2. **Integration Tests**: Multiple components together (medium speed)
3. **End-to-End Tests**: Full system through UI/API (slowest)

**Ratio Guidelines:**
- Unit Tests: 70% (many, fast)
- Integration Tests: 20% (some, medium)
- End-to-End Tests: 10% (few, slow)

**Key Points:**
- **Testing Pyramid**: Many unit tests, fewer integration tests, few E2E tests
- **Mocking**: Isolate component being tested
- **Arrange-Act-Assert**: Clear test structure
- **One assertion per test**: Focus on one behavior
- **Fast execution**: Tests run in seconds
- **Independent tests**: No test depends on another
- **Descriptive names**: testGetUser_WhenFound_ReturnsUser
- **Code coverage**: Aim for >80%
- **Test data**: Use builders or factories
- **Edge cases**: Test boundary conditions

```java
// Unit test - Tests UserService independently
@RunWith(SpringRunner.class)  // Enables Spring in tests
@SpringBootTest
public class UserServiceTest {
    
    @Mock                    // Create mock of UserRepository
    private UserRepository userRepository;
    
    @InjectMocks            // Inject mocks into UserService
    private UserService userService;
    
    private User testUser;
    
    // Setup test data before each test
    @Before
    public void setUp() {
        testUser = new User();
        testUser.setId(1L);
        testUser.setName("John");
        testUser.setEmail("john@example.com");
    }
    
    // Test happy path - User found
    @Test
    public void testGetUserById_Success() {
        // Arrange - Setup mock behavior
        when(userRepository.findById(1L))
                .thenReturn(Optional.of(testUser));
        
        // Act - Execute the method being tested
        User result = userService.getUserById(1L);
        
        // Assert - Verify results
        assertNotNull(result);
        assertEquals("John", result.getName());
        assertEquals("john@example.com", result.getEmail());
        
        // Verify mocks were called correctly
        verify(userRepository, times(1)).findById(1L);
    }
    
    // Test error case - User not found
    @Test(expected = ResourceNotFoundException.class)
    public void testGetUserById_NotFound() {
        // Arrange - Mock returns empty
        when(userRepository.findById(99L))
                .thenReturn(Optional.empty());
        
        // Act - Should throw exception
        userService.getUserById(99L);
        
        // Assert - Exception caught by expected attribute
    }
    
    // Test create operation
    @Test
    public void testCreateUser_Success() {
        // Arrange
        CreateUserRequest request = new CreateUserRequest(
                "Jane", "jane@example.com"
        );
        when(userRepository.save(any(User.class)))
                .thenReturn(testUser);
        
        // Act
        UserDTO result = userService.createUser(request);
        
        // Assert
        assertNotNull(result);
        assertEquals(1L, result.getId());
        
        // Verify save was called once with any User
        verify(userRepository, times(1)).save(any(User.class));
    }
}

// Mock Concepts
/*
when(...).thenReturn(...) - Define mock behavior
when(...).thenThrow(...) - Throw exception on mock call
verify(...) - Verify mock was called
any(Class) - Match any argument
Mockito.spy(...) - Partial mock (real + mock)
*/
```

